    <section class="page-text">
        <h1>Travel Photography for Humans</h1>
        <p class="page-intro">
            For travellers and tour operators.
        </p>
        <p>
            You travel. You experience. I photograph the people, places and moments that make the journey yours. You don't have to
            photograph your life while you're living it.
        </p>
        {# </section>
                                                    <section class="page-text"> #}
        <h2>Why have a photographer on your trip?</h2>
        <p>
            When you travel, you are constantly faced with a small dilemma: do I actually experience this moment, or do I stop and
            photograph it?
        </p>
        <p>
            What if you didn't have to choose?
        </p>
        {# </section>
                                            <section class="page-text"> #}
        <h2>What do I do?</h2>
        <p>
            I travel with you and document the journey as it happens — the places, but especially the people, interactions and small
            moments that make that particular trip yours.
        </p>
        <p>
            I work from inside the group, without turning the journey into a photoshoot. I observe, interact and photograph what
            naturally happens along the way.
        </p>
        {# </section>
                                            <section class="page-text"> #}
        <h2>What do you get?</h2>
        <p>
            Professional photographs that tell the story of your journey.
        </p>
        <p>
            Images can be delivered day by day, so you can relive each day while you are still travelling.
        </p>
        <p>
            Short-form motion content can also be produced where useful.
        </p>
        {# </section>
                                            <section class="page-text"> #}
        <h2>For travellers</h2>
        <p>
            Be present. Enjoy the journey. Leave the documenting to me.
        </p>
        <p>
            You come home with photographs that don't just show where you went, but remember what the journey felt like.
        </p>
        {# </section>
                                            <section class="page-text"> #}
        <h2>For tour operators</h2>
        <p>
            Have you ever thought about turning the documentation of the trip into part of the experience you sell?
        </p>
        <p>
            I can join one of your trips and turn it into both a better experience for your guests and a library of authentic
            content for your brand.
        </p>
        <p>
            The result is content that shows what your trips actually feel like — the people, the atmosphere, the encounters and the
            moments that happen along the way.
        </p>
        {# </section>
                                            <section class="page-text"> #}
        <h2>How can it work?</h2>
        <p>
            There are different ways to build photography into a trip:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>photography included as part of the trip experience;</li>
            <li>an optional service offered to participants;</li>
            <li>a hybrid model combining guest photography and content creation for the operator.</li>
        </ul>
        {# </section>
                                            <section class="page-text"> #}
        <h2>Who am I?</h2>
        <p>
            I'm Marco, a photographer based in Venice, Italy, working between reportage, people and travel.
        </p>
        <p>
            I've worked as a photographer on Galactic Expedition trips, including two expeditions in Morocco, documenting the
            experience from inside the group.
        </p>
        {# </section>
                                            <section class="page-text"> #}
        <h2>Let's talk about your next trip.</h2>
        <p>
            If you're a traveller, a tour operator or an agency and this sounds interesting, get in touch.
        </p>
